      body: 'Here is a made-up story to hold the idea. In a village in Samoa a boy named Tavita told his cousins that their grandfather had once pulled a fish as long as a canoe out of the lagoon. The cousins laughed. There was no picture, they said, so it did not happen. Tavita went to the old people on the beach and asked. One had helped haul the net. One had cut the fish and still knew how many families ate from it. One had been a girl of seven and remembered being lifted up to look into its mouth. They had not sat down together to agree on a tale; each told his own piece, and the pieces fit. And his great-uncle, who had always said the old man boasted, went quiet and then admitted he had carried the tail himself. Tavita went back to his cousins. He did not have a picture. He had eleven people who were there, and one of them had not wanted it to be true. "This Jesus hath God raised up, whereof we all are witnesses." (Acts 2:32)',
